{% layout "layouts/base" %}
{%- comment -%}
  The cart page. The route, what is in the cart and what each line costs are
  the shop plugin's (`plugin_page`, described in the plugin's
  `lib/cart-view.ts`); how it looks, and every word on it, are this theme's.

  The page is one visitor's own: Mallok serves it uncached and unindexed.
  Every control is a plain form posting to `plugin_page.action`, so the cart
  works without a script, and the quantity fields carry the minimum order in
  `min` and the most a line may hold in `max` — which the server checks
  again. The last of them sends the cart as a request for a quote.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% block title %}{{ t.cart_title }} — {{ site.name }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
{% assign cart = plugin_page %}
<section class="shell detail cart">
  <header class="detail-head">
    <h1 class="detail-title">{{ t.cart_title }}</h1>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%}
    A change that was refused: said here, above the cart as it still is. The
    buyer was sent to this page with the reason in its address; the plugin
    read the figures from the database and names the reason as a kind. The
    words for it are in the pack, and the number it is about follows them.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if cart.problem %}
  {% assign reason = "problem_" | append: cart.problem.kind %}
  <div class="cart-problem" role="alert" data-problem="{{ cart.problem.kind }}">
    <p><strong>{{ t.cart_refused }}</strong>{% if cart.problem.sku != blank %} <span class="offer-sku">{{ cart.problem.sku }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
    <p>{{ t[reason] }}{% if cart.problem.kind == "below_moq" %} {{ cart.problem.moq }}{% elsif cart.problem.kind == "insufficient_stock" %} {{ cart.problem.available }}{% elsif cart.problem.kind == "quantity_too_large" %} {{ cart.problem.max }}{% endif %}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {%- comment -%}
    What became of the cart when it was sent as a request for a quote. The
    plugin names the inquiry it became, which it looked up for this visitor's
    own cart, or the kind of reason none was made; nothing a person typed
    comes back through the address, so the form below is empty again.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if cart.sent %}
  <div class="cart-sent" role="status">
    <p><strong>{{ t.quote_sent }}</strong> <span class="offer-sku">{{ cart.sent.number }}</span></p>
    <p>{{ t.quote_sent_note }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if cart.inquiry_problem %}
  {% assign reason = "quote_problem_" | append: cart.inquiry_problem.kind %}
  <div class="cart-problem" role="alert" data-problem="inquiry_{{ cart.inquiry_problem.kind }}">
    <p><strong>{{ t.quote_refused }}</strong></p>
    <p>{{ t[reason] }}{% if cart.inquiry_problem.field != blank %}{% assign label = "quote_" | append: cart.inquiry_problem.field %} {{ t[label] }}{% endif %}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if cart.empty %}
  <p class="empty">{{ t.cart_empty }}</p>
  {% if site.kinds.product %}<p class="cart-back"><a class="btn btn-outline" href="{{ site.kinds.product.path }}">{{ t.back_to_catalogue }}</a></p>{% endif %}
  {% else %}
  <ul class="cart-lines">
    {% for line in cart.lines %}
    <li class="cart-line">
      <div class="cart-what">
        {% if line.name != blank %}<p class="cart-name">{% if line.path != blank %}<a href="{{ line.path }}">{{ line.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ line.name }}{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if line.sku != blank %}<p class="offer-sku">{{ line.sku }}</p>{% endif %}
        {%- comment -%}
          What stands in the way of ordering this line as it is. A line whose
          product is gone has no name left, and says only that.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% if line.problem != blank %}
        {% assign reason = "problem_" | append: line.problem %}
        <p class="cart-line-note" data-problem="{{ line.problem }}">{{ t[reason] }}{% if line.problem == "below_moq" %} {{ line.moq }}{% elsif line.problem == "insufficient_stock" %} {{ line.available }}{% elsif line.problem == "quantity_too_large" %} {{ cart.max_quantity }}{% endif %}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% if line.unit_price != blank %}
      <dl class="offer-terms cart-terms">
        <div><dt>{{ t.unit_price }}</dt><dd><span class="price">{{ line.unit_price }}</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>{{ t.line_total }}</dt><dd><span class="price">{{ line.line_total }}</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="cart-controls">
        {% if line.problem != "unavailable" %}
        <form class="offer-buy" method="post" action="{{ cart.action }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="action" value="set">
          <input type="hidden" name="variant" value="{{ line.variant_id }}">
          <label class="offer-qty"><span>{{ t.quantity }}</span><input type="number" name="quantity" min="{{ line.moq }}" step="1"{% if cart.max_quantity %} max="{{ cart.max_quantity }}"{% endif %} value="{{ line.quantity }}" required inputmode="numeric"></label>
          <button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" type="submit">{{ t.update }}{% if line.sku != blank %}<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ line.sku }}</span>{% endif %}</button>
        </form>
        {% endif %}
        <form method="post" action="{{ cart.action }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="action" value="remove">
          <input type="hidden" name="variant" value="{{ line.variant_id }}">
          <button class="cart-remove" type="submit">{{ t.remove }}{% if line.sku != blank %}<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ line.sku }}</span>{% endif %}</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <div class="cart-foot">
    {%- comment -%}
      The currency, chosen here by a form: the page is rendered for this
      visitor on every request, so the server can simply show another one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% if cart.currencies.size > 1 %}
    <form class="currency" method="post" action="{{ cart.action }}" role="group" aria-label="{{ t.currency }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="action" value="currency">
      {% for code in cart.currencies %}<button type="submit" name="currency" value="{{ code }}" aria-pressed="{% if code == cart.currency %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">{{ code }}</button>{% endfor %}
    </form>
    {% endif %}
    {% if cart.subtotal != blank %}<p class="cart-subtotal"><span>{{ t.subtotal }}</span> <span class="price">{{ cart.subtotal }}</span></p>{% endif %}
    <p class="cart-note">{{ t.cart_note }}</p>
    {% if site.kinds.product %}
    <div class="buy-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="{{ site.kinds.product.path }}">{{ t.back_to_catalogue }}</a>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The cart, sent as one request for a quote: a plain form, like every
    other control here. A line without a price does not stand in its way —
    that is what a quote is for — and any other problem does, so the form is
    offered only when the plugin says the cart can go as it stands.

    Each field carries the server's own rule: `required`, the length the
    plugin allows, for the address the pattern it is held to, and for the
    name that it is not only spaces. A browser then refuses what the server
    would, and the server's refusal — which comes back with the fields
    empty — is not something a person meets for what they typed.

    The last field is one no person sees or reaches: whatever fills it in is
    not one, and the plugin stores nothing for it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if cart.inquiry_action != blank %}
  {% if cart.can_inquire %}
  <form class="quote-form" method="post" action="{{ cart.inquiry_action }}" aria-labelledby="quote-form-title">
    <h2 class="quote-form-title" id="quote-form-title">{{ t.quote_form_title }}</h2>
    <p class="quote-form-intro">{{ t.quote_form_intro }}</p>
    <div class="quote-form-pair">
      <label>{{ t.quote_name }}<input type="text" name="name" required pattern=".*\S.*" maxlength="200" autocomplete="name"></label>
      <label>{{ t.quote_email }}<input type="email" name="email" required maxlength="320" pattern="[\p{L}\p{N}._+'\-]+@[\p{L}\p{N}\-]+(\.[\p{L}\p{N}\-]+)+" autocomplete="email"></label>
    </div>
    <div class="quote-form-pair">
      <label>{{ t.quote_company }} <span class="quote-form-optional">{{ t.optional }}</span><input type="text" name="company" maxlength="200" autocomplete="organization"></label>
      <label>{{ t.quote_phone }} <span class="quote-form-optional">{{ t.optional }}</span><input type="tel" name="phone" maxlength="60" autocomplete="tel"></label>
    </div>
    <label>{{ t.quote_message }} <span class="quote-form-optional">{{ t.optional }}</span><textarea name="message" rows="5" maxlength="5000"></textarea></label>
    <p class="quote-form-trap" aria-hidden="true"><label>{{ t.quote_leave_empty }}<input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></p>
    <button class="btn btn-solid" type="submit">{{ t.quote_send }}</button>
  </form>
  {% else %}
  <p class="cart-note quote-form-blocked">{{ t.quote_fix_first }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endblock %}
